This print shows a toad patrolling the garden in the hunt for food.
Various bugs are in the area, hoping not to catch the toad's attention.

The bugs on the print include a representative from each of the four sub-phyla of the phylum Arthropoda: Crustacea (woodlouse), Hexapoda (earwig, beetle), Myriapoda (centipede), Chelicerata (harvestman).

Toads are lucky. On a good day you can find everything in this scene in my back garden.

This is a variable edition print. The bugs are hand-stamped.

